  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>N</mi></math> be a function such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>m</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>n</mi></mfenced></math> for every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math>&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math> is equal to :"
  },
